Package: PedAscertain
Title: Simulate and ascertain pedigrees with a rare genetic variant linked to disease onset
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Eloise", "Cook", , "eejc143@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Simulates pedigrees who have a dominant rare genetic variant and are at risk 
    of onset of a disease linked to the variant e.g. certain rare tumour risk syndromes (RTRS) 
    are linked to an increased probability of rare cancer. The founder is always a carrier of 
    the rare variant and individuals who are carriers of the rare variant have a different 
    hazard for disease onset to non-carriers, modified using the gentetic relative 
    risk (GRR) as a hazard multiplier. The user can specify 
    ascertainment requirements for the pedigree, 
    and pedigrees are ascertained by a proband who experiences disease onset within a 
    specified time interval. This package was created for use in a simulation study 
    to assess different ascertainment bias correcting methods in the event history analysis
    of RTRS, which is currently in the process of being published.
    The pedigree simulation is based on methodology 
    used for the SimRVPedigree package described by Nieuwoudt et al. (2018).
